# Dock catalog, read by zdock (the desktop's separate "shell"): one icon per
# entry in its bar along the top of the screen.  The window server's
# right-click menu keeps its OWN catalog, /usr/hr/etc/apps: the two lists are
# independent, so the dock can carry fewer icons than the menu offers apps
# (or different ones).
# One line per icon:  name:execpath:multi:icon:X,Y:args  (all but the first
# two optional)
#   name        dock-icon label AND the app's title base: by convention it
#               equals the title the program declares in its HRAPP, which is
#               how the dock matches windows to this entry (a mismatch and
#               the icon never reads as running).
#   execpath    program; run with these arguments (plus -P X,Y first)
#   multi       1 = may open many copies (middle click starts another);
#               0 = single instance (a second click switches to it)
#   icon        .icn under /usr/hr/icons.  EVERY entry's icon is always
#               visible: sitting high with the name beneath while nothing
#               runs, pressed (dropped down, no name) while the app has a
#               window or a launch is in flight.  Left click launches or
#               switches to the app's topmost window.  Missing artwork gets
#               the generic icon0.icn.
#   X,Y         where a dock launch puts the window (top-left of the frame);
#               left out, the server places it.  Keep Y clear of the dock
#               strip (the top ~70px) or the new window opens under it.
#   args        extra command-line arguments, blank-separated, appended
#               after -P at launch
#
# The window itself -- title, size, icon while hidden, whether it may be
# stretched -- is NOT configured here: the application declares it at
# start-up (hr_open, see inc/hrapp.h), so a program can also be run straight
# from a shell.
#
# A line starting with '@' is a WIDGET:  @name:execpath[:click][:args]  --
# a small resident program (zwclock, zwmem, ...) the dock starts itself,
# drawing live content in an icon-sized cell at the RIGHT end of the bar
# (first @ line = rightmost cell; at most 4).  Widgets have no icon; a
# crashed one is restarted, a few times, then given up on.  They are not
# meant to be run from a shell.
# The click field makes the cell a button:
#   Title=/path   left click gets the dock-icon verb for that app -- switch
#                 to it when it runs, launch it when it does not -- so the
#                 app's own icon can be taken off the bar;
#   *             left click opens the server's "Switch to..." dialog.
#
# The rc script /usr/hr/etc/rc runs at desktop start-up: it starts the dock,
# and anything else that should be genuinely RESIDENT from power-on.
Shell:/usr/hr/bin/zterm:1:term.icn:48,88
Files:/usr/hr/bin/zfile:1:file.icn:120,100
Editor:/usr/hr/bin/zedit:1:edit.icn:80,84
Mail:/usr/hr/bin/zmail:0:mail.icn:100,120
Manual:/usr/hr/bin/zman:0:man.icn:180,140
Calculator:/usr/hr/bin/zcalc:0:calc.icn:600,180
Printer:/usr/hr/bin/zprint:0:printer.icn:380,300
Puzzle:/usr/hr/bin/zpuzzle:0:puzzle.icn:700,300
Maze:/usr/hr/bin/zmaze:0:maze.icn:620,300
@Time:/usr/hr/bin/zwclock:Clock=/usr/hr/bin/zclock
@Memory:/usr/hr/bin/zwmem:Monitor=/usr/hr/bin/zmon
@Programs:/usr/hr/bin/zwwin:*
